      "level": 2,
      "content": "Local Variables"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Variables defined inside a function are local to it, they are not accessible outside the function."
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "c",
      "content": "1#include <stdio.h>\n2\n3void addNumbers(int n1, int n2) {\n4\n5  int result = n1 + n2;\n6}\n7\n8int main() {\n9\n10  // Error: 'result' is undeclared\n11  printf(\"%d\", result);\n12\n13  return 0;\n14}"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "Standard Library Functions"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "C provides various built-in functions that we can directly use in our program by including the required header file."
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "c",
      "content": "1#include <stdio.h> // for I/O operations\n2#include <math.h> // for math operations\n3\n4int main() {\n5\n6  double squareRoot = sqrt(81);\n7  printf(\"%.2lf\", squareRoot);    // 9.00\n8\n9  return 0;\n10}"
    },
